, 			{
				"box" : 				{
					"id" : "obj-9",
					"linecount" : 52,
					"maxclass" : "comment",
					"numinlets" : 1,
					"numoutlets" : 0,
					"patching_rect" : [ 888.0, 537.0, 154.0, 717.0 ],
					"presentation" : 1,
					"presentation_linecount" : 31,
					"presentation_rect" : [ 840.0, 433.0, 299.0, 435.0 ],
					"text" : "ALIEN sound, based off the Wow! signal: an extraterrestrial burst in the radio frequency detected in 1977 with no known origin (maybe the aliens....?) \n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wow!_signal\n\noriginally built for 7-speaker spatialization, mixed down to stereo for this documentation\n\n\n- audio is a series of 6 sharp impulses\n- each impulse's amplitude is scaled by the intensity of each datapoint of the Wow! signal\n\n- variable parameters: pitch, relay speed, and decay\n\n- pitch: change pitch of sound. highest pitch is 1440.4556 Hz, corresponding to the Wow! signal's radio frequency of 1440.4556 MHz\n\n- relay speed: change the timing between impulses. Shortest time is 72 milliseconds, longest is 720 milliseconds, corresponding to the 7.2 second duration of the Wow! signal\n\n- decay tail: timing of 'noise tail' after each impulse. (No correspondance to Wow! signal, just for funsies and texture)\n\n- press the big BANG to trigger the sound!\n\n"
				}

			}
